h"],["thesis","tuhinga whakapae","too-HEE-ngah fah-kah-PIE"],["diploma","tīwhikete","tee-fee-KEH-teh"],["seminar","wānanga","wah-NAH-ngah"],["entrance exam","whakamātautau urunga","fah-kah-mah-tow-TOW oo-ROO-ngah"],["application","tono","TOH-noh"],["student card","kāri akonga","KAH-ree ah-KOH-ngah"],["faculty","kāhui ako","KAH-hoo-ee AH-koh"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","ako","AH-koh"],["to teach","whakaako","fah-kah-AH-koh"],["to ask","pātai","PAH-tie"],["to answer","whakautu","fah-kah-OO-too"],["to repeat","kōrero anō","KOH-reh-roh AH-noh"],["to understand","mārama","MAH-rah-mah"],["to remember","maumahara","mow-mah-HAH-rah"],["to forget","wareware","wah-reh-WAH-reh"],["to explain","whakamārama","fah-kah-MAH-rah-mah"],["to practise","whakaharatau","fah-kah-hah-rah-TOW"],["to pass an exam","paahi i te whakamātautau","PAH-hee ee teh fah-kah-mah-tow-TOW"],["to fail an exam","rahua i te whakamātautau","rah-HOO-ah ee teh fah-kah-mah-tow-TOW"],["to write down","tuhi iho","TOO-hee EE-hoh"],["to listen","whakarongo","fah-kah-ROH-ngoh"],["to read aloud","pānui ā-reo","PAH-noo-ee AH REH-oh"],["to think","whakaaro","fah-kah-AH-roh"],["to count","tatau","tah-TOW"],["to spell","tuhi pūtia","TOO-hee POO-tee-ah"],["to translate","whakamāori","fah-kah-MAH-oh-ree"],["to graduate","whiwhi tohu","FEE-fee TOH-hoo"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Māori has a dual \"we\" (two people) and a plural \"we\" (three or more), and each comes in two kinds: \"tāua / tātou\" includes the listener, \"māua / mātou\" excludes the listener. There is no he / she difference: \"ia\" means both."],"rows":[["I","ahau (au)","AH-how (OW)"],["you (one)","koe","KWAY"],["he / she","ia","EE-ah"],["we two (with you)","tāua","TAH-oo-ah"],["we (with you)","tātou","TAH-toh"],["we (without you)","mātou","MAH-toh"],["you (plural)","koutou","KOH-toh"],["they","rātou","RAH-toh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","he akonga ahau","heh ah-KOH-ngah AH-how"],["you are tall","kei te teitei koe","kay teh TAY-tay KWAY"],["she is my older sister","ko tōku tuakana wahine ia","koh TOH-koo too-ah-KAH-nah wah-HEE-neh EE-ah"],["we are friends","he hoa tātou","heh HOH-ah TAH-toh"],["they are teachers","he kaiako rātou","heh kie-AH-koh RAH-toh"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Nouns do not change. Use \"te\" (the) for one and \"ngā\" (the) for many: te pukapuka (the book), ngā pukapuka (the books). Use \"ētahi\" for \"some\": ētahi pukapuka."],"rows":[["the book","te pukapuka","teh poo-kah-POO-kah"],["the books","ngā pukapuka","ngah poo-kah-POO-kah"],["the child","te tamaiti","teh tah-MIE-tee"],["the children","ngā tamariki","ngah tah-mah-REE-kee"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","kotahi te whare, ngā whare","KOH-tah-hee teh FAH-reh, ngah FAH-reh"],["one book, books","kotahi te pukapuka, ngā pukapuka","KOH-tah-hee teh poo-kah-POO-kah, ngah poo-kah-POO-kah"],["one cat, cats","kotahi te ngeru, ngā ngeru","KOH-tah-hee teh NGEH-roo, ngah NGEH-roo"],["two books","e rua ngā pukapuka","eh ROO-ah ngah poo-kah-POO-kah"],["the children","ngā tamariki","ngah tah-mah-REE-kee"]]},{"id":"to-be-he-ko-kei","title":"To be: he, ko, kei","text":["Māori has no verb \"to be\". Use \"he\" before a noun (he kaiako ahau, a teacher I), \"ko\" for a name or identity, and \"kei\" for places (kei te kura ahau). An adjective can stand first with \"kei te\"."],"rows":[["I am a teacher","he kaiako ahau","heh kie-AH-koh AH-how"],["this is a book","he pukapuka tēnei","heh poo-kah-POO-kah TEH-nay"],["I am at home","kei te kāinga ahau","kay teh KAH-ee-ngah AH-how"],["I am tall","kei te teitei ahau","kay teh TAY-tay AH-how"]],"ex":[["I am a student","he akonga ahau","heh ah-KOH-ngah AH-how"],["you are tired","kei te ngenge koe","kay teh NGEH-ngeh KWAY"],["he is a doctor","he taote ia","heh TAH-oh-teh EE-ah"],["we are happy","kei te harikoa tātou","kay teh hah-ree-KOH-ah TAH-toh"],["they are at home","kei te kāinga rātou","kay teh KAH-ee-ngah RAH-toh"]]},{"id":"having-he-t-ku","title":"Having: he ... tāku","text":["To say \"I have\", Māori says \"a ... mine\": he motokā tāku (a car mine). Use \"tōku\" for things that are part of you, like family and body (o-class), and \"tāku\" for things you own or do (a-class)."],"rows":[["I have a car","he motokā tāku","heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-koo"],["you have a car","he motokā tāu","heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-oo"],["he / she has a car","he motokā tāna","heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-nah"],["I do not have","kāore he ... tāku","KAH-oh-reh heh ... TAH-koo"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","he tuakana tāne tōku","heh too-ah-KAH-nah TAH-neh TOH-koo"],["I have a car","he motokā tāku","heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-koo"],["I do not have time","kāore he wā tōku","KAH-oh-reh heh wah TOH-koo"],["there is a problem","he raruraru kei konei","heh rah-roo-RAH-roo kay KOH-nay"],["there is no water","kāore he wai","KAH-oh-reh heh WHY"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Verbs do not change for person. Put \"kei te\" before the verb for now: kei te kai ahau (I am eating). Without \"kei te\", the verb has no time."],"rows":[["I am eating","kei te kai ahau","kay teh KIE AH-how"],["you are eating","kei te kai koe","kay teh KIE KWAY"],["he / she is eating","kei te kai ia","kay teh KIE EE-ah"],["we are eating","kei te kai tātou","kay teh KIE TAH-toh"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","kei te kai ahau i te parāoa","kay teh KIE AH-how ee teh pah-RAH-oh-ah"],["you are reading a book","kei te pānui koe i te pukapuka","kay teh PAH-noo-ee KWAY ee teh poo-kah-POO-kah"],["she works in a bank","kei te mahi ia i te peeke","kay teh MAH-hee EE-ah ee teh PEH-eh-keh"],["we drink tea","kei te inu mātou i te tī","kay teh EE-noo MAH-toh ee teh TEE"],["they are sleeping","kei te moe rātou","kay teh MOH-eh RAH-toh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb comes first. The order is verb, subject, object: \"kei te pānui ahau i te pukapuka\" (reading I the book). \"I\" marks the object."],"rows":[["I read a book","kei te pānui ahau i te pukapuka","kay teh PAH-noo-ee AH-how ee teh poo-kah-POO-kah"],["he drinks tea","kei te inu ia i te tī","kay teh EE-noo EE-ah ee teh TEE"],["a big house","he whare nui","heh FAH-reh NOO-ee"],["a new car","he motokā hou","heh moh-toh-KAH HOH"]],"ex":[["I read a book","kei te pānui ahau i te pukapuka","kay teh PAH-noo-ee AH-how ee teh poo-kah-POO-kah"],["he drinks tea","kei te inu ia i te tī","kay teh EE-noo EE-ah ee teh TEE"],["we go to school","kei te haere mātou ki te kura","kay teh HIGH-reh MAH-toh kee teh KOO-rah"],["they eat bread","kei te kai rātou i te parāoa","kay teh KIE RAH-toh ee teh pah-RAH-oh-ah"],["the teacher writes","kei te tuhi te kaiako","kay teh TOO-hee teh kie-AH-koh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"kāore\" before the verb, and \"e\" after the subject: kāore ahau e hiahia (I do not want). For the past, use \"i\": kāore ahau i kai (I did not eat). For \"there is none\", use \"kāore he\"."],"rows":[["I do not go","kāore au e haere","KAH-oh-reh OW eh HIGH-reh"],["you do not go","kāore koe e haere","KAH-oh-reh KWAY eh HIGH-reh"],["he / she does not go","kāore ia e haere","KAH-oh-reh EE-ah eh HIGH-reh"],["it is not good","kāore e pai","KAH-oh-reh eh PIE"]],"ex":[["I want","e hiahia ana ahau","eh hee-AH-hee-ah AH-nah AH-how"],["I do not want","kāore au e hiahia","KAH-oh-reh OW eh hee-AH-hee-ah"],["I speak English","kei te kōrero Ingarihi ahau","kay teh KOH-reh-roh ee-ngah-REE-hee AH-how"],["I do not speak English","kāore au e kōrero Ingarihi","KAH-oh-reh OW eh KOH-reh-roh ee-ngah-REE-hee"],["I like it","he pai ki ahau","heh pie kee AH-how"],["I do not like it","kāore e pai ki ahau","KAH-oh-reh eh pie kee AH-how"],["she is here","kei konei ia","kay KOH-nay EE-ah"],["she is not here","kāore ia i konei","KAH-oh-reh EE-ah ee KOH-nay"],["I have a car","he motokā tāku","heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-koo"],["I do not have a car","kāore he motokā tāku","KAH-oh-reh heh moh-toh-KAH TAH-koo"],["I understand","kei te mārama ahau","kay teh MAH-rah-mah AH-how"],["I do not understand","kāore au e mārama","KAH-oh-reh OW eh MAH-rah-mah"],["we are tired","kei te ngenge tātou","kay teh NGEH-ngeh TAH-toh"],["we are not tired","kāore tātou e ngenge","KAH-oh-reh TAH-toh eh NGEH-ngeh"],["he works on Sundays","ka mahi ia i te Rātapu","kah MAH-hee EE-ah ee teh RAH-tah-poo"],["he does not work on Sundays","kāore ia e mahi i te Rātapu","KAH-oh-reh EE-ah eh MAH-hee ee teh RAH-tah-poo"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Raise your voice at the end, or begin with \"he\": \"He pai tēnei?\" (Is this good?). To answer, say \"āe\" (yes) or \"kao\" (no), or repeat the verb."],"rows":[["Do you go?","kei te haere koe?","kay teh HIGH-reh KWAY"],["Is it good?","he pai?","heh PIE"],["Is it right?","he tika?","heh TEE-kah"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","nāu tēnei pukapuka?","NAH-oo TEH-nay poo-kah-POO-kah"],["are they here?","kei konei rātou?","kay KOH-nay RAH-toh"],["do you like tea?","he pai ki a koe te tī?","heh pie kee ah KWAY teh TEE"],["is it cold?","kei te makariri?","kay teh mah-kah-REE-ree"],["do you speak English?","kei te kōrero Ingarihi koe?","kay teh KOH-reh-roh ee-ngah-REE-hee KWAY"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words usually come at the start or take the place of the answer."],"rows":[["who","wai","WHY"],["what","aha","AH-hah"],["where","hea","HEH-ah"],["when","āhea","AH-heh-ah"],["why","nā te aha","nah teh AH-hah"],["how","pēhea","PEH-heh-ah"],["how much","e hia","eh HEE-ah"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","ko wai tō ingoa?","koh WHY toh ee-NGOH-ah"],["who is he?","ko wai ia?","koh WHY EE-ah"],["where do you live?","kei hea koe e noho ana?","kay HEH-ah KWAY eh NOH-hoh AH-nah"],["when is the lesson?","āhea te akoranga?","AH-heh-ah teh ah-koh-RAH-ngah"],["why are you late?","nā te aha koe i tōmuri ai?","nah teh AH-hah KWAY ee TOH-moo-ree eye"],["how much is it?","e hia te utu?","eh HEE-ah teh OO-too"],["which book?","tēhea pukapuka?","TEH-heh-ah poo-kah-POO-kah"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Two kinds of \"my\": \"tōku\" (parts of you, family, home) and \"taku\" (things you own or choose, like a pencil or a plan). Your: tō / tāu. His, her: tōna / tāna. Their: tō rātou / ā rātou."],"rows":[["my body (o-class)","tōku tinana","TOH-koo tee-NAH-nah"],["my book (a-class)","taku pukapuka","TAH-koo poo-kah-POO-kah"],["your book","tāu pukapuka","TAH-oo poo-kah-POO-kah"],["his / her book","tāna pukapuka","TAH-nah poo-kah-POO-kah"]],"ex":[["my phone","taku waea","TAH-koo WAH-eh-ah"],["your house (formal)","tō koutou whare","toh KOH-toh FAH-reh"],["his sister","tōna tuahine","TOH-nah too-ah-HEE-neh"],["I like music","he pai ki ahau te puoro","heh pie kee AH-how teh poo-OH-roh"],["I love football","e aroha ana ahau ki te whutupaoro","eh ah-ROH-hah AH-nah AH-how kee teh foo-too-PAH-oh-roh"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Māori shows respect with \"koutou\" (you, plural) for one person, with \"e te rangatira\" (sir, chief) and with \"tēnā koa\" (please). There is no formal verb form."],"rows":[["sir","e te rangatira","eh teh rah-ngah-TEE-rah"],["madam","e kui","eh KOO-ee"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","kei te pēhea koe?","kay teh PEH-heh-ah KWAY"],["how are you? (formal)","kei te pēhea koutou?","kay teh PEH-heh-ah KOH-toh"],["where are you going? (informal)","kei te haere koe ki hea?","kay teh HIGH-reh KWAY kee HEH-ah"],["where are you going? (formal)","kei te haere koutou ki hea?","kay teh HIGH-reh KOH-toh kee HEH-ah"],["please sit down (formal)","noho, tēnā koa","NOH-hoh, TEH-nah KOH-ah"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Verbs do not change. Past: put \"i\" before the verb (i kai ahau, I ate). Future: put \"ka\" before the verb (ka kai ahau, I will eat)."],"rows":[["I ate","i kai ahau","ee KIE AH-how"],["I will eat","ka kai ahau","kah KIE AH-how"],["I will go tomorrow","ka haere ahau āpōpō","kah HIGH-reh AH-how ah-poh-POH"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","inanahi, i ngenge ahau","ee-nah-NAH-hee, ee NGEH-ngeh AH-how"],["I will study tomorrow","ka ako ahau āpōpō","kah AH-koh AH-how ah-poh-POH"],["we went to the park","i haere mātou ki te papa rēhia","ee HIGH-reh MAH-toh kee teh PAH-pah REH-hee-ah"],["I saw him","i kite ahau i a ia","ee KEE-teh AH-how ee ah EE-ah"],["she wrote a letter","i tuhi ia i tētahi reta","ee TOO-hee EE-ah ee TEH-tah-hee REH-tah"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["A command is the plain verb: haere mai (come). To forbid, put \"kaua e\" before the verb: kaua e haere (do not go)."],"rows":[["come!","haere mai!","HIGH-reh MY"],["wait!","tatari!","tah-TAH-ree"],["do not go","kaua e haere","KOW-ah eh HIGH-reh"],["please wait","tatari, tēnā koa","tah-TAH-ree, TEH-nah KOH-ah"]],"ex":[["come here","haere mai ki konei","HIGH-reh MY kee KOH-nay"],["do not come here","kaua e haere mai ki konei","KOW-ah eh HIGH-reh MY kee KOH-nay"],["sit down","noho iho","NOH-hoh EE-hoh"],["do not sit down","kaua e noho","KOW-ah eh NOH-hoh"],["be quiet","noho marie","NOH-hoh MAH-ree-eh"],["do not be late","kaua e tōmuri","KOW-ah eh TOH-moo-ree"],["open the door","whakatuwheratia te tatau","fah-kah-too-feh-RAH-tee-ah teh tah-TOW"],["close the window","katia te matapihi","KAH-tee-ah teh mah-tah-PEE-hee"],["listen to me","whakarongo mai ki ahau","fah-kah-ROH-ngoh MY kee AH-how"],["do not worry","kaua e māharahara","KOW-ah eh MAH-hah-rah-hah-rah"],["speak slowly","kōrero marie","KOH-reh-roh MAH-ree-eh"],["wait a moment","tatari mō tētahi wā","tah-TAH-ree moh TEH-tah-hee WAH"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["\"Ka taea\" (can), \"me\" (must) and \"hiahia\" (want) are the key words. Ka taea e au te... (it is possible for me to...), me haere ahau (I must go)."],"rows":[["I can swim","ka taea e au te kauhoe","kah TIE-ah eh OW teh kow-HOH-eh"],["I must go","me haere ahau","meh HIGH-reh AH-how"],["I want to go","e hiahia ana ahau ki te haere","eh hee-AH-hee-ah AH-nah AH-how kee teh HIGH-reh"],["may I?","ka taea?","kah TIE-ah"]],"ex":[["I can swim","ka taea e au te kauhoe","kah TIE-ah eh OW teh kow-HOH-eh"],["I cannot swim","kāore e taea e au te kauhoe","KAH-oh-reh eh TIE-ah eh OW teh kow-HOH-eh"],["can you help me?","ka taea e koe te āwhina i ahau?","kah TIE-ah eh KWAY teh AH-fee-nah ee AH-how"],["we must go","me haere tātou","meh HIGH-reh TAH-toh"],["we must not go","kaua tātou e haere","KOW-ah TAH-toh eh HIGH-reh"],["I want to eat","e hiahia ana ahau ki te kai","eh hee-AH-hee-ah AH-nah AH-how kee teh KIE"],["I do not want to eat","kāore au e hiahia ki te kai","KAH-oh-reh OW eh hee-AH-hee-ah kee teh KIE"],["you can come","ka taea e koe te haere mai","kah TIE-ah eh KWAY teh HIGH-reh MY"],["you cannot come","kāore e taea e koe te haere mai","KAH-oh-reh eh TIE-ah eh KWAY teh HIGH-reh MY"],["she wants to study","e hiahia ana ia ki te ako","eh hee-AH-hee-ah AH-nah EE-ah kee teh AH-koh"],["I must work today","me mahi ahau i tēnei rā","meh MAH-hee AH-how ee TEH-nay RAH"],["you must not run","kaua koe e oma","KOW-ah KWAY eh OH-mah"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Māori uses small words: \"i\" (at, in), \"ki\" (to), \"kei\" (is at), \"kei runga i\" (on), \"kei raro i\" (under), \"kei roto i\" (inside), \"kei te taha o\" (next to), \"e tata ana ki\" (near)."],"rows":[["in the house","kei roto i te whare","kay ROH-toh ee teh FAH-reh"],["on the table","kei runga i te tēpu","kay ROO-ngah ee teh TEH-poo"],["under the table","kei raro i te tēpu","kay RAH-roh ee teh TEH-poo"],["at school","kei te kura","kay teh KOO-rah"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kei runga te pukapuka i te tēpu","kay ROO-ngah teh poo-kah-POO-kah ee teh TEH-poo"],["the cat is under the table","kei raro te ngeru i te tēpu","kay RAH-roh teh NGEH-roo ee teh TEH-poo"],["I am at school","kei te kura ahau","kay teh KOO-rah AH-how"],["I am at home","kei te kāinga ahau","kay teh KAH-ee-ngah AH-how"],["the shop is next to the bank","kei te taha o te peeke te toa","kay teh TAH-hah oh teh PEH-eh-keh teh TOH-ah"],["the park is near the station","e tata ana te papa rēhia ki te teihana","eh TAH-tah AH-nah teh PAH-pah REH-hee-ah kee teh TAY-hah-nah"],["we meet in the morning","ka hui tātou i te ata","kah HOO-ee TAH-toh ee teh AH-tah"],["the lesson is at nine","ā te iwa karaka te akoranga","ah teh EE-wah KAH-rah-kah teh ah-koh-RAH-ngah"],["the key is in the bag","kei roto te kī i te pēke","kay ROH-toh teh KEE ee teh PEH-keh"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Māori adds \"ake\" for \"more\": nui ake (bigger), pai ake (better). For \"than\", use \"i\": pai ake tēnei i tērā. For \"the most\", use \"rawa atu\": nui rawa atu."],"rows":[["big, bigger","nui, nui ake","NOO-ee, NOO-ee AH-keh"],["good, better","pai, pai ake","PIE, PIE AH-keh"],["the biggest","nui rawa atu","NOO-ee RAH-wah AH-too"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","nui, nui ake, nui rawa atu","NOO-ee, NOO-ee AH-keh, NOO-ee RAH-wah AH-too"],["small, smaller, the smallest","iti, iti ake, iti rawa atu","EE-tee, EE-tee AH-keh, EE-tee RAH-wah AH-too"],["this is better than that","pai ake tēnei i tērā","PIE AH-keh TEH-nay ee TEH-rah"],["this is worse than that","kino ake tēnei i tērā","KEE-noh AH-keh TEH-nay ee TEH-rah"],["she is taller than me","teitei ake ia i ahau","TAY-tay AH-keh EE-ah ee AH-how"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","nui ake a Tashkent i a Samarkand","NOO-ee AH-keh ah tash-KENT ee ah sa-mar-KAND"],["it is the cheapest","ko tēnei te mea utu iti rawa atu","koh TEH-nay teh MEH-ah OO-too EE-tee RAH-wah AH-too"],["the same as","ōrite ki","OH-ree-teh kee"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[["I am hungry","kei te hiakai ahau","kay teh hee-AH-kie AH-how"],["I am thirsty","kei te hiainu ahau","kay teh hee-AH-ee-noo AH-how"],["I am cold","kei te makariri ahau","kay teh mah-kah-REE-ree AH-how"],["it is raining","kei te ua","kay teh OO-ah"]],"ex":[["he is a teacher","he kaiako ia","heh kie-AH-koh EE-ah"],["you (plural) are students","he akonga koutou","heh ah-KOH-ngah KOH-toh"],["I am happy","kei te harikoa ahau","kay teh hah-ree-KOH-ah AH-how"],["she is at school","kei te kura ia","kay teh KOO-rah EE-ah"],["you are my friend","he hoa koe nōku","heh HOH-ah KWAY NOH-koo"],["it is cold","kei te makariri","kay teh mah-kah-REE-ree"],["I study English","kei te ako ahau i te reo Ingarihi","kay teh AH-koh AH-how ee teh REH-oh ee-ngah-REE-hee"],["he teaches maths","kei te whakaako ia i te pāngarau","kay teh fah-kah-AH-koh EE-ah ee teh PAH-ngah-row"],["they work every day","ka mahi rātou ia rā","kah MAH-hee RAH-toh EE-ah RAH"],["is this your book?","nāu tēnei pukapuka?","NAH-oo TEH-nay poo-kah-POO-kah"],["are they here?","kei konei rātou?","kay KOH-nay RAH-toh"],["do you like tea?","he pai ki a koe te tī?","heh pie kee ah KWAY teh TEE"],["what time is it?","ko te hia karaka?","koh teh HEE-ah KAH-rah-kah"],["whose book is this?","nā wai tēnei pukapuka?","nah WHY TEH-nay poo-kah-POO-kah"],["how old are you?","e hia ō tau?","eh HEE-ah oh TOW"],["how do you say it?","me pēhea e kī ai?","meh PEH-heh-ah eh KEE eye"],["your book (formal)","tā koutou pukapuka","tah KOH-toh poo-kah-POO-kah"],["their house","tō rātou whare","toh RAH-toh FAH-reh"],["my phone","taku waea","TAH-koo WAH-eh-ah"],["excuse me, sir","aroha mai, e te rangatira","ah-ROH-hah MY, eh teh rah-ngah-TEE-rah"],["please sit down (formal)","noho, tēnā koa","NOH-hoh, TEH-nah KOH-ah"],["come here (informal)","haere mai ki konei","HIGH-reh MY kee KOH-nay"],["yesterday I was tired","inanahi, i ngenge ahau","ee-nah-NAH-hee, ee NGEH-ngeh AH-how"],["I will study tomorrow","ka ako ahau āpōpō","kah AH-koh AH-how ah-poh-POH"],["we went to the park","i haere mātou ki te papa rēhia","ee HIGH-reh MAH-toh kee teh PAH-pah REH-hee-ah"]]}],"name":"Māori (Te Reo Māori)","id":"mi","flag":"nz","note":""}